sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-01> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch14-01: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.80" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.803"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Monophyly of a named class is a standard phylogenetic question, and public trees already place most species that taxonomists assign to classes. Molecular data are largely independent of the morphological class diagnoses Darwin knew, which gives the test real discriminating power. Checking the historical membership of each class is days to weeks of work, not a new data collection." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Take each traditional class of animals and plants as a set of included species and test whether those species form a single clade on a tree built from molecular characters. The claim is confirmed if each such class is monophyletic or is a single clade once historically excluded members are accounted for, and refuted if a class is composed of two or more unrelated clades." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Some traditional classes were defined by ecology or by the absence of traits and are paraphyletic, so membership has to be fixed from the historical concept before the test.", "Horizontal gene transfer in fungi, plants and protists can make different genes disagree about a single progenitor for a class.", "The deepest nodes of several invertebrate classes are still sensitive to taxon sampling and to the choice of model." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch14-01 by Grok 4.7: 0.8" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-01> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-01--grok--operationalizability> .
